x86_64-linux  two differences, neither about the conversion. The constructors are COMDAT: cxx1 emits one defined inside its class as an ordinary definition where clang emits it linkonce_odr in a section the collector does not read. And `ranked(const S &)` and `overEllipsis(...)` are static functions this case declares to be *lost* by overload resolution - clang discards a static function nothing calls, and cxx1 emits it. Neither is what this case is about, which is which candidate wins, and run.sh checks that on all three machines by the value each returns.
arm64-darwin  two differences, neither about the conversion. The constructors are COMDAT: cxx1 emits one defined inside its class as an ordinary definition where clang emits it linkonce_odr in a section the collector does not read. And `ranked(const S &)` and `overEllipsis(...)` are static functions this case declares to be *lost* by overload resolution - clang discards a static function nothing calls, and cxx1 emits it. Neither is what this case is about, which is which candidate wins, and run.sh checks that on all three machines by the value each returns.
